--- body ---
## Context

This ticket was ruled a monster on 2026-09-02 and is now the TRACKER for the
attachment-format estate. It bundled at least three sign-off units into six
Actions: authoring a nine-format fixture matrix, which needs no machine;
measuring that matrix through a live Zotero, which needs an idle instance and
the local API to itself; carrying the resulting policy to the author, which is
his ruling and nobody else's; and implementing that ruling in `SPEC.md`, in
R17's reporting and in acceptance coverage. Its prose also carried the
dependency chain in narrative rather than in `Blocked-by`, so nothing machine
readable said that Action 5 cannot start before Action 4.

Three children, each sized to one sign-off unit, each blocked by its real
prerequisite and never by this tracker.

The partition boundary is the author's ruling. Everything on one side of it is
authorship and observation, which an agent can finish alone; everything on the
other side implements a decision that does not exist yet. The measurement child
sits on the boundary because putting the evidence to the author is what produces
the ruling. That is why the estate splits into three and not two: the fixture
matrix is separable from the measurement by a second boundary, the machine —
ticket 0599 needs no Zotero at all, and it was the only part of this ticket that
could run on the night it was filed, while a full-library build held the local
API.

The candidate policy this estate tests is stated once, in ticket 0600, and is
not repeated here.

## Children

- **ticket 0599** — build the fixture matrix and the content-capability
  classifier that decides a format from bytes rather than from a filename,
  with the misleading-extension control that makes the MIME-not-extension
  invariant mechanical. Machine-free. Blocked-by: nothing.
- **ticket 0600** — import the matrix through a real Zotero, reindex, probe
  `/fulltext` and the full-text control plugin, record content types and
  terminal states, and put the candidate policy to the author for a ruling in
  `DECISIONS.md`. Blocked-by: ticket 0599. Labelled `needs-human`: it needs a
  live, idle Zotero and it ends in the author's decision, neither of which an
  agent supplies.
- **ticket 0601** — carry the ruled policy into `SPEC.md`, add the
  per-attachment extraction-route/reason field and R17's counts in the ruled
  vocabulary, and add acceptance coverage matching the ruled matrix.
  Blocked-by: ticket 0600.

Wave order is the blocking chain: 0599, then 0600, then 0601. There is no
parallelism to find here, and pretending otherwise is what made this a monster.

## Invariants

Stated once, here, and inherited by every child:

- **Metadata coverage never depends on body-format support.** A format whose
  body cannot be read is still a record that answers on its metadata.
- **Unsupported is a terminal, reported state**, with a stored reason. It is not
  a failure, and it is not an indexed body.
- **The policy is MIME/capability based, not an extension allow-list.**
- **No converter joins the default path by implication.** This estate does not
  authorize LibreOffice, Pandoc, Tika or a cloud converter, and no test it
  produces invokes a network or a document-conversion service. A future local
  converter needs its own ruling over security, resource budgets, fidelity and
  derivation identity.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] ticket 0599 closed
- [ ] ticket 0600 closed
- [ ] ticket 0601 closed
- [ ] the integration review: with all three closed, re-read the children's
      diffs together, run the full suite, and verify that the ruled matrix is
      one policy rather than three — that every format named in `DECISIONS.md`
      has a row in the acceptance coverage, that no format is eligible on its
      extension anywhere in the chain, and that the `.doc` gap is recorded as a
      gap wherever it is relied on
